hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16057","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said, al-Murajja ibn Raja al-Yashkuri narrated to us, he said, Salm ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, he said, I heard Sawadah ibn al-Rabi saying, I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, and he ordered for me some camels, then he said to me: When you return to your house, order them to feed their young animals well, and order them to trim their nails, and not to wound with them the udders of their cattle when they milk."
